# PR #331 Review

## Scope
- Reviewed PR diff via "'`gh pr diff 331`
- Reviewed PR metadata via `gh pr view 331 --json title,body,files`
- PR body does **not** contain a `Task: @task-ref` trailer, so this was a pure code review (AC/spec trailer checks skipped per instructions)

## Findings

### MUST-FIX
1. `src/sessions/store.ts:1049`
   Week grouping is incorrect while labeled as ISO week format.
   - Current implementation uses local time (`getFullYear`, `getDay`, `new Date(year, 0, 1)`) and a Sunday-based formula.
   - This misclassifies UTC timestamps near day/year boundaries in US time zones.
   - Example: `2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z` can be grouped into `2025-W53` depending on local TZ.
   - Impact: analytics results for `kspec session log stats --by-week` are wrong for boundary dates.
   - Fix direction: compute ISO week-year in UTC (ISO-8601 week rules), not local calendar week math.

### SHOULD-FIX
1. `tests/session-log-stats.test.ts:321`
   Week grouping tests only validate string shape (`/''^'"\\d{4}-W\\d{2}"'$/`) and do not verify correctness.
   - This allows incorrect week logic to pass.
   - Add concrete assertions for known boundary dates (start/end of year and week transitions), including UTC-boundary timestamps.

## Posted Review
- Attempted to submit `REQUEST_CHANGES` as instructed, but GitHub API rejected it: cannot request changes on own PR (`HTTP 422`).
- Posted equivalent review as `COMMENT` with inline comments instead.
MD
